---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro'
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro'
import { site } from '../data/site'
const controller = site.legalName || site.name
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy Notice | Twin Tech-sudo" description="How Twin Tech-sudo handles website enquiries, analytics and personal information.">
  <SiteHeader /><main><article class="insight legal-page"><header><span class="page-kicker">// PRIVACY</span><h1>Privacy notice</h1><p>How we collect, use and protect personal information.</p><div><time datetime="2026-10-17">Last updated 17 October 2026</time></div></header><div class="insight-body">
    <p class="insight-intro">{controller} is the controller of personal information described in this notice. Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    <section><span>01</span><h2>Information we collect</h2><p>When you contact us, we may receive your name, email address, organisation, project requirements and anything else you choose to include. We also retain ordinary business records created while discussing, contracting for and delivering services.</p></section>
    <section><span>02</span><h2>Why we use it</h2><p>We use enquiry information to respond, take steps you request before entering a contract, prepare proposals, deliver services, manage client relationships, keep appropriate financial and legal records, protect our systems and establish or defend legal claims. Depending on the activity, the lawful basis is steps before a contract, performance of a contract, legal obligation or our legitimate interests in operating and protecting the business.</p></section>
    <section><span>03</span><h2>Analytics and cookies</h2><p>Optional Google Analytics is loaded only after you accept analytics cookies. It helps us understand aggregate use of the website. You can decline it or change your choice using Cookie settings in the footer. See the <a href="/cookies/">cookie notice</a> for details.</p></section>
    <section><span>04</span><h2>Who receives information</h2><p>We may use carefully selected providers for email, hosting, analytics, accounting, professional advice and secure business administration. They receive only the information needed for their role. We do not sell personal information. Where a provider processes information outside the UK, we assess and use an appropriate legal transfer safeguard where required.</p></section>
    <section><span>05</span><h2>How long we keep it</h2><p>Unsuccessful enquiries are normally reviewed for deletion after 24 months. Client, contractual, tax and accounting records may be retained for up to seven years after the relationship ends, or longer where a legal obligation or live dispute requires it. We delete or anonymise information when it is no longer needed.</p></section>
    <section><span>06</span><h2>Security</h2><p>We use access controls, multi-factor authentication, device security and appropriate backups. No internet service can promise absolute security, but we review controls in proportion to the information and risks involved.</p></section>
    <section><span>07</span><h2>Your rights</h2><p>UK data protection law may give you rights to access, correct, erase or restrict your information, object to certain uses, and receive portable information. Contact us to exercise a right. You may also complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.</p></section>
    <section><span>08</span><h2>Changes</h2><p>We will update this notice when our services or information practices change and will publish the revised date on this page.</p></section>
  </div></article></main><SiteFooter />
</SiteLayout>
